      "claim": "An adult human skull is a rigid structure that cannot deform to reduce its dimensions.",
      "evidence": "Unlike a fetal skull which has unfused fontanelles and sutures allowing for molding, an adult skull is fully ossified with fused sutures, making it mechanically rigid and incapable of significant compression without fracture.",
      "weight": 0.3,
