      "id": 3,
      "claim": "The human birth canal (pelvis) is a rigid bony ring that cannot expand to accommodate an object larger than its anatomical limits.",
      "evidence": "The pelvis is a stable bony structure. While soft tissues can stretch, the bony ring does not expand significantly without catastrophic fracture, which would not constitute a physiological 'passing through' of the canal.",
